  "limitations": [
    "RUN-02 creates pure in-memory plan snapshots and inert approval requests; RUN-05 owns action persistence, idempotency-key derivation, claims, replay recovery, dispatch, and receipts.",
    "RUN-08 owns durable approval hydration and projection persistence; ORCH-08 owns approval-barrier consumption; RUN-10 owns decision authority and scope evaluation.",
    "ORCH-09 owns durable audit events, ORCH-06 owns runtime retries and budgets, and DEL-04 owns database migrations and seeding.",
    "The no-network gate proves the pure planner has no connector authority and failed validation produces zero IDs or clock reads; crash recovery remains a persistence concern.",
    "Trusted runtime composition must atomically supply the content hash and records from the same validated CompiledCatalog plus its validated connector registry; the planner cannot recompute the compiler's full content hash from its structural subset, so coordinated forged metadata under a valid label is outside this contract.",
    "The existing exact-action v1 hash was a pre-release, unpersisted development contract; RUN-02 finalizes its projection and locks structural, semantic, destination, and exact golden vectors before any RUN-05 persistence exists."
  ]
